# The module imports `p::*` and declares its own `CoproInstr [NbInstr]` while
# the package also has a `CoproInstr`.  Surelog (before 47f59c3ec7) bound the
# module's parameter to the PACKAGE's: the 65-bit x 2 table was laid out as
# 73-bit x 3 and every field read landed off its element (CVA6
# compressed_instr_decoder decoded nothing).  The miter against read_slang
# fails with the old Surelog and passes with the fix.
read_uhdm slpp_all/surelog.uhdm
hierarchy -check -top dut
flatten; proc; opt -fast; async2sync; setundef -undriven -zero
rename dut gold
design -stash gold
read_slang dut.sv --top dut
hierarchy -check -top dut
flatten; proc; opt -fast; async2sync; setundef -undriven -zero
rename dut gate
design -stash gate
design -copy-from gold -as gold gold
design -copy-from gate -as gate gate
miter -equiv -flatten -make_assert gold gate miter
hierarchy -top miter
sat -verify -prove-asserts -seq 1 -set-init-zero miter
